The assert statement checks if the height (`r.lin`) of the rectangle `r` is positive. If the assert condition is true, then nothing happens. But if the condition is false (that is, `r.lin` is not greater than 0), then it asserts that the error has occurred. This is useful for debugging and can also be used as a sanity check.
